{"kind":"request","text":"S4 scope choice before source: the current MCP Apps Visibility section uses nested _meta.ui.visibility. A model-only tool requires the host to reject app-originated tools/call. Primary specification: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps/blob/main/specification/2026-01-26/apps.mdx#visibility . At main7177, packages/mcp/src/service.ts:928-929 builds ordinary write descriptors; catalogue.ts:248-249 builds native act descriptors. views/tools.ts:51-53 marks app-only tools, and view_act at86-89 plus declared inputs at102-109 intentionally submit retained native actions. Alternative A: make ordinary and dynamic writes model-only while retaining the captured view_act/input tools. Cards keep buttons/forms, but their scripts can still invoke those bounded writes, so this needs an explicit exemption from the literal request. Alternative B: make every native-writing tool model-only, including view_act/input. Card reads and navigation remain, but buttons and forms cannot submit. That choice also needs clear disabled actions or the existing chat handoff; view_act currently bundles local read/review actions too. Which behavior do you rule for S4? No patch or executable check has run.","body":{"conditions":"Rule whether S4 closes all native-writing Card tools or explicitly exempts captured view_act and declared input tools. No Git artifact: scope ruling only.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}